/// <summary>
/// Adds a resilience handler optimized for streaming (SSE) requests.
/// Disables per-attempt and total request timeouts to prevent
/// cutting off long-running streams, while keeping retry and circuit breaker.
/// </summary>
public static IHttpClientBuilder AddCisharpaiStreamingResilienceHandler(this IHttpClientBuilder builder)
{
    builder.AddStandardResilienceHandler(options =>
    {
        options.AttemptTimeout = new HttpTimeoutStrategyOptions 
        { 
            Timeout = Timeout.InfiniteTimeSpan 
        };
        options.TotalRequestTimeout = new HttpTimeoutStrategyOptions 
        { 
            Timeout = Timeout.InfiniteTimeSpan 
        };
        // Retry and circuit breaker remain at default settings
    });
    return builder;
}
```

## Context
The current `AddCisharpaiResilienceHandler()` sets:
- `AttemptTimeout`: 60s
- `TotalRequestTimeout`: 90s

These are appropriate for non-streaming requests but would terminate any stream longer than 60-90 seconds. The streaming handler removes these limits.

## Usage
Callers who know they will use streaming can configure their HttpClient:
```csharp
services.AddHttpClient<IStreamingChatFeature>("streaming-client")
    .AddCisharpaiStreamingResilienceHandler();
```

Or it can be used by provider DI registrations that support streaming.

